{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 30, :comments ["<b>Therefore he called his name Edom.</b> When they saw that he was so entirely given over to his defective occupation, unlike the way of man, that he did not recognize the stew except by its color. <b>He called his name Edom.</b> In the imperative — that is: make yourself red and be dyed red in the gulping down of the red stuff."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {0 "Reading הַלְעָטַת (the stuffing/gulping) as Sforno writes it; the word is rare and refers to force-feeding or greedy eating, here applied to the lentil stew."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:31:41.927247023Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}